            {
              "id": "m-010",
              "cells": [
                {
                  "id": "m-011",
                  "text": {
                    "en": [
                      {
                        "text": "Minimum wage"
                      }
                    ],
                    "zh": [
                      {
                        "text": "最低工資"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "m-012",
                  "text": {
                    "en": [
                      {
                        "text": "The government sets a legal lowest wage that employers may pay. If it is set above the equilibrium wage, the quantity of labour supplied exceeds the quantity demanded and unemployment results."
                      }
                    ],
                    "zh": [
                      {
                        "text": "政府訂定僱主可支付的法定最低工資。若最低工資高於均衡工資，勞工供應量會超過需求量，引致失業。"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "m-013",
              "cells": [
                {
                  "id": "m-014",
                  "text": {
                    "en": [
                      {
                        "text": "Price ceiling"
                      }
                    ],
                    "zh": [
                      {
                        "text": "價格上限"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "m-015",
                  "text": {
                    "en": [
                      {
                        "text": "The government sets a legal highest price that sellers may charge. If it is set below the equilibrium price, the quantity demanded exceeds the quantity supplied and a shortage results."
                      }
                    ],
                    "zh": [
                      {
                        "text": "政府訂定賣方可收取的法定最高價格。若價格上限低於均衡價格，需求量會超過供應量，引致短缺。"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "m-016",
              "cells": [
                {
                  "id": "m-017",
                  "text": {
                    "en": [
                      {
                        "text": "Subsidy to producers"
                      }
                    ],
                    "zh": [
                      {
                        "text": "生產者補貼"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "m-018",
                  "text": {
                    "en": [
                      {
                        "text": "The government pays producers a sum for each unit sold. This lowers their cost of production, shifts the supply curve to the right, lowers the price and raises the quantity traded."
                      }
                    ],
                    "zh": [
                      {
                        "text": "政府就每單位售出的貨品向生產者付款。這降低生產成本，令供應曲線右移，價格下降，成交量上升。"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
